# "You may discard your hand. If you do, draw three cards" with no cards in hand: Bot1 empties the hand on turn 1 and
# returns Phyrexian Dragon Engine from its own graveyard with Unearth the sorcery, not the keyword. It enters from
# Bot1's graveyard, so it triggers; saying yes discards a hand of nothing, which is still discarding the hand, and
# Bot1 draws three. Returned by a spell rather than its own unearth, it has no haste.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Faithless Looting
Phyrexian Dragon Engine
Unearth
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Mountain
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Phyrexian Dragon Engine; Mountain)
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Unearth.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Phyrexian Dragon Engine)
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.Keywords = DoubleStrike
? Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.SummoningSick = True

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Unearth; Faithless Looting; Mountain; Black Lotus
